    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.starter\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI have toggleterm bound to `[[<C-\\>]]` and it's always popping up along with mini.starter.\r\nI've looked more into it and [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/06eddfd8d6341e6c4f53ec9ae109a376a566329d/lua/mini/starter.lua#L1284) seems to be the issue.\r\n\r\nI think a check for the current mode ought to fix this.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.8.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nuse mini.starter with something bound to `<C-\\>`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`<C-\\>` not executing\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`<C-\\>` executing",
